# The generated coach pack is a build artifact. The rubric beside it, coach/rubric.md, is
# a REVIEWED artifact and is committed.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH ON PURPOSE. A bare `coach/` rule would match a folder of
# that name at ANY depth, and — worse — ignoring the whole folder would silently drop every
# future file added beside the rubric out of `git status` and `git add -A`. That failure is
# invisible at the moment it happens: the work is simply never committed, and it surfaces
# much later as missing. The rule names the generated subfolder only, so anything else that
# lands in coach/ stays visible.
/coach/pack/

# Isolated copies of the tool that boundary tests spawn, so they can plant directory links
# without touching the real coach/ folder. Created and removed per test; ignored so a
# crashed run cannot leave one in `git status`.
/.tool-fixture-*/
